5) Osteopenia / fall risk (important with anticoagulation)
- Ask about bone density follow-up, vitamin D and calcium, and fall-risk mitigation (since being on apixaban increases bleeding consequences of falls).
- Discuss safe pain management alternatives for back pain (avoid NSAIDs if possible while anticoagulated).

6) Red flags to report urgently
- New/worsening chest pain, sudden shortness of breath, sudden weakness or slurred speech, syncope, significant bleeding, sudden severe headache.

7) Practical checklist to bring to the visit
- Current meds with doses (including OTCs, supplements, topical meds).
- Recent BP log or readings.
- Recent lab results if you have them (creatinine, CBC, lipids).
- A list of symptoms and specific questions (use the questions above).
- Ask Dr. Wilson whether he recommends a referral to Colorado Cardiology and, if yes, what specific information he will send.

