While you answer, here are practical items to prepare for the visit and guidance on hypertension and cardiology referral.

What to bring to your appointment with Dr. James Wilson
- A complete current medication list (prescription, OTC, supplements), doses and timing (especially apixaban, metoprolol, iron or anticoagulant-related meds, NSAIDs).
- A home blood pressure log (at least a week if possible) with morning and evening readings. If you don’t have one, start taking BP twice daily for 7 days.
- Recent labs or lab results (creatinine/eGFR, CBC/hemoglobin, electrolytes, liver tests, lipid panel).
- A list of symptoms (dizziness, lightheadedness when standing, palpitations, chest pain, bleeding events).
- Any prior cardiac tests (ECG, echo, stress test) if available.

Important tests to request (given apixaban, anemia, osteopenia, and hypertension)
- CBC (to quantify anemia and trend hemoglobin)
- Basic metabolic panel (creatinine, electrolytes) and eGFR — apixaban dosing and safety depend on kidney function
